BT 1 0 0 1 0 207.888 Tm 1.1344 Tw 18 TL /F4 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (2016 Bar Q: A railroad track of the Philippine National Railway \(PNR\) is located near a) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.061455 Tw (busy intersection of Puyat Avenue and Osme\361a Highway. One afternoon, the intersection) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.380857 Tw (was heavily congested, as usual. Juan, the driver of a public utility jeepney \(PUJ\), drove) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.3144 Tw (onto the railroad tracks but could go no farther because of the heavy traffic at the) Tj T* 0 Tw 4.387385 Tw (intersection. After the jeepney stopped right on the railroad track, it was hit and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.7715 Tw (overturned by a PNR train, resulting in the death of Kim, a passenger of the PUJ, and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.099385 Tw (injuries to Juan and his other passengers. Juan, the injured passengers and Kim's family) Tj T* 0 Tw .848 Tw (sued the PNR for damages for its negligence. It was established that the steel pole barrier) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.27275 Tw (before the track was broken, and that the PNR had the last clear chance of avoiding the) Tj T* 0 Tw .66975 Tw (accident. On the other hand, the PNR raised the defense that the track is for the exclusive) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.376 Tw (use of the train and that motorists are aware that it is negligence per se to stop their) Tj T* 0 Tw (vehicles on the tracks. Decide the case and explain. \(5%\)) Tj T* ET
