BT 1 0 0 1 0 297.804 Tm .89925 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The PNR answers to the family of Kim and to the injured passengers, though Juan personal ) Tj T* 0 Tw .653143 Tw (recovery suffers his own contributory fault, because the broken barrier and the last clear chance ) Tj T* 0 Tw (keep the operator liable while driver fault never travels to the riders.) Tj ( ) Tj T* .534353 Tw (Under Art. 1756 of the Civil Code, death of or injury to passengers presumes the carrier at fault ) Tj T* 0 Tw .185538 Tw (unless it proves the extraordinary diligence of Arts. 1733 and 1755. Under the crossing-diligence ) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.672 Tw (rule, the rail operator must keep bells, lights, barriers, and watchmen working at known ) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.73025 Tw (congested crossings, and the train with the final opportunity to stop must use it. In LRTA v. ) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.182769 Tw (Navidad \(G.R. No. 145804, 2003\), the Court measured train and station safety by utmost ) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.313231 Tw (diligence and held the duty non-delegable. Driver negligence is never imputed to the riding ) Tj T* 0 Tw (passenger, so the passenger claim survives though the jeepney driver shared blame.) Tj ( ) Tj T* .096 Tw (Here, the PNR track lay near the busy intersection of Puyat Avenue and Osmena Highway where ) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.356 Tw (congestion was usual, and Juan drove his public utility jeepney onto the rails but could go no ) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.73625 Tw (farther because of heavy traffic. The jeepney stopped on the track and the PNR train hit and ) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.004571 Tw (overturned it, killing passenger Kim and injuring Juan and the other passengers. The steel pole ) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.2785 Tw (barrier before the track was broken, and the PNR had the last clear chance of avoiding the ) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.594 Tw (accident. The exclusive-track argument cannot excuse a broken warning device at a known ) Tj T* 0 Tw (choke point, and Juan breached his own motorist duty by entering rails he could not clear.) Tj  T* 