BT 1 0 0 1 0 261.804 Tm 1.96 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The bus company answers the injured passengers in full, since its own want of diligence) Tj T* 0 Tw (keeps the presumption unrebutted regardless of what the truck driver did.) Tj  T* 1.33725 Tw (Under Art. 1756 of the Civil Code, injury to passengers presumes the carrier at fault unless it) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.699385 Tw (proves the extraordinary diligence of Arts. 1733 and 1755. Under that diligence, the operator) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.911429 Tw (must hire licensed and tested drivers, supervise them in service, and inspect brakes and gear) Tj T* 0 Tw .4845 Tw (before and during the run. In LRTA v. Navidad \(G.R. No. 145804, 2003\), the Court held carrier) Tj T* 0 Tw (safety duty non-delegable and measured crew and equipment fitness by utmost diligence.) Tj  T* .411429 Tw (Here, the company hired an unlicensed driver without road test and skipped brake inspection for) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.37925 Tw (a month, and the bus with worn pads rammed a truck. Hiring without license or test breaches) Tj T* 0 Tw .812 Tw (selection diligence and running a month without brake checks breaches inspection diligence, so) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.390154 Tw (no concrete precaution rebuts the presumption. The truck fault, if proved, divides the ultimate) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.811 Tw (loss between the operators through contribution, yet division never delays or defeats the) Tj T* 0 Tw (passenger recovery.) Tj  T* 2.648 Tw (The passengers therefore collect from their carrier upon the presumption, and the company) Tj T* 0 Tw (pursues the truck operator separately for its share.) Tj T* ET
