BT 1 0 0 1 0 279.804 Tm 1.9608 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The suitcase claimant recovers on proof of turnover with loss at arrival, while the laptop) Tj T* 0 Tw (claimant recovers only on proof of carrier fault, because custody fixes the burden for each piece.) Tj  T* .172286 Tw (Under Art. 1733 of the Civil Code, extraordinary diligence governs goods in carrier custody, and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.364308 Tw (loss outside the five Art. 1734 causes presumes fault unless extraordinary diligence is proved.) Tj T* 0 Tw .830824 Tw (Under the baggage rule, a tagged piece handed to the carrier for the hold rides under the goods) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.316615 Tw (rules, while a hand-carried piece kept by the passenger stays under proved-fault rules. In) Tj T* 0 Tw .236308 Tw (Regional Container Lines of Singapore v. The Netherlands Insurance Co. \(Phils.\), Inc. \(G.R. No.) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.464 Tw (168151, 2009\), the Court kept custody and the fault presumption alive through unloading and) Tj T* 0 Tw (required proof of diligence rather than mere pointing at another handler.) Tj  T* 1.46475 Tw (Here, the tagged suitcase was checked into the hold and vanished before arrival, so it rode in) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.803692 Tw (carrier custody and its disappearance raises the presumption unless the carrier proves an Art.) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.417538 Tw (1734 excuse or extraordinary diligence. The laptop stayed in the overhead bin in passenger) Tj T* 0 Tw .04575 Tw (custody, and the passenger left it to use the lavatory before the snatching, so no presumption runs) Tj T* 0 Tw (and the passenger must show the loss came through employee fault or want of due precautions.) Tj  T* 1.220571 Tw (The first claim therefore succeeds on custody and loss alone unless rebutted, while the second) Tj T* 0 Tw (needs specific carrier fault proved against the operator.) Tj T* ET
