BT 1 0 0 1 0 261.804 Tm 1.1168 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: She collects no moral damages, because a clean delay with prompt apology and full refund) Tj T* 0 Tw (draws only actual loss and the refund already quenches it.) Tj  T* 1.8952 Tw (Under Art. 2220 of the Civil Code, breach of contract draws moral damages only where the) Tj T* 0 Tw .9824 Tw (defendant acted fraudulently or in bad faith. Under Art. 2217 of the Civil Code, moral anguish) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.927692 Tw (must be proximately tied to a wrongful manner and never to mere disappointment over) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.494909 Tw (consequence. Under the package award in Unsworth Transport International \(Phils.\), Inc. v.) Tj T* 0 Tw .2248 Tw (Court of Appeals \(G.R. No. 166250, 2010\), delay with interest and fees but without wilful injury) Tj T* 0 Tw (carried no moral sum.) Tj  T* .981231 Tw (Here, the line delayed the bride three hours through plain mismanagement, apologized at once,) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.3408 Tw (and refunded the fare in full. The refund quenches the pecuniary part and the prompt apology) Tj T* 0 Tw 4.369 Tw (negates the spite that moral requires. Her ruined photographs reflect genuine pain over) Tj T* 0 Tw .494769 Tw (consequence rather than Art. 2217 anguish proximately tied to a fraudulent or bad-faith manner.) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.525455 Tw (The counter-reading that deep disappointment alone opens moral fails because clean breach) Tj T* 0 Tw (never does.) Tj  T* (The claim therefore ends with the refunded fare and no moral award.) Tj T* ET
