BT 1 0 0 1 0 261.804 Tm .0936 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The carrier loses the fight, because the fifty thousand pesos indemnity stands beside the moral) Tj T* 0 Tw (award and admitted recklessness opens exemplary correction as well.) Tj  T* 1.048 Tw (Under Art. 2206 of the Civil Code, death gives moral damages to the spouse with descendants) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.388571 Tw (and ascendants for mental anguish by reason of the death alone, without separate fraud proof.) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.672 Tw (Under Art. 2232 of the Civil Code, wanton, fraudulent, reckless, oppressive, or malevolent) Tj T* 0 Tw .433714 Tw (conduct opens exemplary damages in contract. Under Sps. Cruz v. Sun Holidays, Inc. \(G.R. No.) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.061 Tw (186312, 2010\), a package-tour drowning drew the indemnity with one hundred thousand pesos) Tj T* 0 Tw (moral with one hundred thousand pesos exemplary on presumed recklessness.) Tj  T* 2.695714 Tw (Here, the carrier pays the fifty thousand pesos death indemnity but fights the one hundred) Tj T* 0 Tw .4512 Tw (thousand pesos moral award by arguing no fraud attended the accident. The death came from its) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.062 Tw (own admittedly reckless overloading, and presumed fault stands unrebutted on these facts. The) Tj T* 0 Tw .6072 Tw (counter-reading that moral needs fraud fails because the Art. 2206 death door and the Art. 2232) Tj T* 0 Tw (recklessness door each open without fraud.) Tj  T* 4.219636 Tw (The indemnity therefore stands beside moral damages with exemplary correction on the) Tj T* 0 Tw (recklessness shown.) Tj T* ET
